  q(GOV,'Which professional guide, the DMBOK, describes a widely used framework for data management and governance?','DAMA International’s Data Management Body of Knowledge',['The ICD-10-CM manual','The HIPAA Privacy Rule','The Joint Commission standards manual'],'C','DAMA-DMBOK covers areas such as data quality, security, metadata and architecture.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'Code tables that list allowed values, such as state abbreviations or gender codes, are called:','Reference data',['Transaction data','Audit logs','Metadata about users'],'D','Managing reference data centrally keeps values consistent across systems.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'Old records that are rarely used are moved to lower-cost storage but kept for retention rules. What is this?','Archiving',['Purging','Encryption','Data mining'],'A','Archived records can still be retrieved if needed for care, audits or legal reasons.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'Master data management creates a single, trusted version of each patient or provider record. What is this version often called?','The golden record',['The legal hold','The audit trail','The designated record set'],'B','The golden record combines the best data from several systems about the same person.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'A hospital hires experts to try to break into its systems to find weaknesses before attackers do. What is this?','Penetration testing',['Usability testing','Data profiling','Phishing'],'C','Findings from penetration tests guide fixes to reduce security risks.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which plan describes how staff will detect, contain and recover from a cyberattack?','An incident response plan',['A strategic plan','A data dictionary','A retention schedule'],'D','Practicing the plan with drills helps staff respond quickly during a real attack.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Why should hospitals install software updates from vendors promptly?','Updates fix security flaws that attackers can exploit',['Updates slow systems','Updates delete old records','Updates are required for billing'],'A','Many ransomware attacks use known flaws that had patches available.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which tool lets a hospital enforce passwords, encryption and remote wiping on staff smartphones that access PHI?','Mobile device management (MDM)',['A PACS','An encoder','A disease registry'],'B','If a phone is lost, MDM can erase hospital data to prevent a breach.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Under HIPAA, a statistician certifies that the risk of re-identifying people in a data set is very small. Which de-identification method is this?','Expert determination',['Safe harbor','A limited data set','Encryption in transit'],'C','Expert determination is the alternative to removing all 18 safe harbor identifiers.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Staff working from home connect to hospital systems through an encrypted tunnel over the internet. What is this tool?','A virtual private network (VPN)',['A firewall log','A cloud data warehouse','Single sign-on (SSO) portal'],'D','VPNs protect data sent between remote users and the hospital network.',ZC),
  q(ETH,'A de-identified data set is combined with public voter records, and some patients can be identified. What risk does this show?','Re-identification',['Data lineage','Alert fatigue','Inter-rater reliability'],'A','Combining data sources can reveal identities, so data sharing needs careful controls.',ZC),
  q(ETH,'A health informatics professional takes courses to keep up with new privacy laws and technology. Which ethical duty is this?','Maintaining professional competence',['Paternalism','Data custodianship','Conflict of interest'],'B','Professional codes expect members to keep their knowledge and skills current.',ZC),
  q(RES,'Researchers survey whoever is in the clinic waiting room that day. What type of sample is this?','A convenience sample',['A stratified random sample','A simple random sample','A systematic sample'],'C','Convenience samples are easy to collect but may not represent the population.',WH),
  q(RES,'Staff perform better simply because they know they are being observed in a study. What is this called?','The Hawthorne effect',['The placebo effect','Recall bias','Regression to the mean'],'D','Observation itself can change behavior, which can make an intervention look better than it is.',WH),
  q(RES,'A study enrolls only adults aged 40 to 65 with type 2 diabetes and excludes pregnant patients. What are these rules called?','Inclusion and exclusion criteria',['Hypotheses','Confounders','Dependent variables'],'A','Clear criteria define who the results apply to and help protect participants.',WH),
  q(RES,'Before a study is published in a journal, independent experts review its methods and conclusions. What is this process?','Peer review',['Informed consent','Data mining of results','Institutional Review Board approval'],'B','Peer review helps catch weak methods and unsupported claims, though it cannot catch every error.',WH),
  q(RES,'Results from a study of young adults at one urban hospital may not apply to older rural patients. Which concern is this?','Limited generalizability (external validity)',['Low reliability of the survey','Poor internal validity from bias','Low statistical power from small samples'],'C','External validity is how well results apply to other people and settings.',WH),
  q(RES,'In a case-control study, which measure of association is usually calculated?','The odds ratio',['The relative risk','The incidence rate','The attack rate'],'D','Case-control studies start with outcome status, so risk cannot be measured directly.',WH),
  q(EMER,'Connected devices such as smart infusion pumps and wireless monitors send data to hospital systems. What is this network called?','The Internet of Medical Things (IoMT)',['Blockchain','A data warehouse for analytics','Single sign-on (SSO) access'],'A','Connected devices improve data flow but add new targets for cyberattacks.',ZC),
  q(EMER,'Software apps that are prescribed to treat conditions such as insomnia or substance use disorder are called:','Digital therapeutics',['Patient portals','Encoders','Practice management systems'],'B','Many digital therapeutics are reviewed by the FDA like medical devices.',ZC)
